## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of streaming data structures, heap-based algorithms, and amortized complexity analysis in a real-time processing context.

## Key Concepts
- **Two-heap streaming median:** A max-heap stores the lower half; a min-heap stores the upper half.
- **Rebalancing invariant:** Heap sizes differ by at most one, ensuring the median is accessible in O(1).
- **Time complexity:** O(log n) per element for insertion plus O(log n) for rebalancing.
- **Space complexity:** O(n), proportional to total elements seen.

## Code Example
```javascript
insert(x) {
  if (L.isEmpty() || x <= L.max()) {
    L.insert(x);
  } else {
    R.insert(x);
  }
  rebalance();
}

rebalance() {
  if (L.size() > R.size() + 1) {
    R.insert(L.extractMax());
  } else if (R.size() > L.size() + 1) {
    L.insert(R.extractMin());
  }
}

getMedian() {
  if (L.size() > R.size()) return L.max();
  if (R.size() > L.size()) return R.min();
  return (L.max() + R.min()) / 2;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design streaming data structures with sliding windows, handling batched updates, and rigorous amortized analysis. Also probes correctness under expirations and the practical choice between exact maintenance vs rebuilds.

## Key Concepts
- Sliding window frequency tables, heap with lazy deletion, batch amortized analysis, memory locality, worst-case scenarios.

## Code Example
```javascript
class TopFreqWindow {
  constructor(W) { this.W = W; this.cnt = new Map(); this.queue = []; this.heap = new MaxHeap(); }
  batchInsert(vals) {
    for (const v of vals) {
      this.queue.push(v);
      this.cnt.set(v, (this.cnt.get(v) || 0) + 1);
      this.heap.push({ value: v, count: this.cnt.get(v) });
    }
    this.expireIfNeeded();
  }
  expireIfNeeded() {
    while (this.queue.length > this.W) {
      const old = this.queue.shift();
      const c = (this.cnt.get(old) || 0) - 1;
      if (c <= 0) this.cnt.delete(old); else this.cnt.set(old, c);
      this.heap.push({ value: old, count: c });
    }
  }
  top1() {
    while (true) {
      const t = this.heap.peek(); if (!t) return null;
      if ((this.cnt.get(t.value) || 0) === t.count) return t.value;
      this.heap.pop();
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for approximate top-k with space constraints?
- Analyze behavior under adversarial burst patterns and discuss optimizations.

